- op: discuss  # 32a3
  at: '2026-05-05T00:57:05Z'  # 32a3
  by: agent  # 32a3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 32a3
  clock: 2  # 32a3
  nonce: 32a3  # 32a3
  message: "## Framing question: does this need its own ADR?\n\nADR-0024 is the template for axis declarations on dataclass FIELDS. The three shipped instantiations (ADR-0023 Edge.edge_type, ADR-0027 Symbol.kind, ADR-0028 Edge.evidence_type) all share these assumptions: one field name + multiple legal values, values bucketed into sub-axes within one conceptual concern, single-string schema property with x-axis-of-values, four-phase migration (registry → consumer → producer → closure).\n\naxis_meta_keys.py parallels these in some ways but breaks the model in others. The framing question for implementation is: does this work need its own ADR (call it ADR-0029), or is it a natural extension of ADR-0024?\n\n## Analysis\n\n**Structural similarities (favors \"natural extension\"):**\n- Same registry / drift linter / property test / by-axis view artifact set\n- Same L3 producer-coherence machinery (the producer_coherence.py walker generalizes from `Edge.create(..., field=...)` to `Edge.create(..., meta={\"key\": ...})` — same AST shape, different argument position)\n- Same consumer-discipline goal: don't hardcode key names; query the registry\n\n**Structural differences (favors \"needs its own ADR\"):**\n\n1. **Topology inverts.** A field has ONE name + MANY legal values. A meta dict has MANY legal KEYS, each with ITS OWN value space. Each meta key IS an axis (or sub-axis), not a value within an axis.\n\n2. **Schema representation is different.** Field axes get `type: string` + `x-axis-of-values`. The meta dict gets `additionalProperties` shape with the registry surfacing as a key namespace; per-key value spaces each get their own (recursive) axis declaration if multi-value.\n\n3. **Validation is two-level.** Both the KEY and the VALUE matter. `meta[\"framework_role\"] = \"consumer\"` requires `framework_role` to be in the key registry AND `consumer` to be in the framework_role value space.\n\n4. **Lifecycle reverses.** ADR-0024 axes pre-exist; the four-phase migration tightens an already-loose existing field. Meta keys are CREATED by the producer migration (Phase 3 fold residue from ADR-0027/0028) — they don't pre-exist as a leaky field; they EMERGE as the canonical home for the residue. So the \"registry first, then migrate consumers/producers\" sequencing is partially scrambled.\n\n5. **Multi-axis per dict.** Edge.meta may carry `framework_dispatch` AND `call_construct` AND others. ADR-0024 is one-axis-per-field. The meta-key registry must accommodate multiple distinct axes living in the same physical dict.\n\nThe five differences are real and load-bearing. Per ADR-0024's own conceptual-leak audit philosophy, conflating field-axis and dict-key-axis under one ADR risks exactly the kind of cross-axis smuggling ADR-0028 was created to prevent.\n\n## Recommendation: Option C — extend ADR-0024 with a one-paragraph scope clarification, AND open ADR-0029 as the first worked example for the meta-key namespace\n\nThis mirrors the existing pattern: ADR-0024 is the template, and each per-axis ADR (ADR-0023, ADR-0027, ADR-0028) is a concrete worked example. ADR-0029 would be the first worked example for the meta-key parallel namespace.\n\n**Concrete proposal for ADR-0029:**\n- Declare the meta-key namespace convention. Each meta key is its own axis (or sub-axis); the registry is its namespace.\n- Establish axis_meta_keys.py as the registry module.\n- Each entry: name + purpose + value-space pointer (which may itself be an ADR-0024-shaped axis declaration).\n- Initial seed: post-Phase-3 fold residues from ADR-0027 + ADR-0028 (framework_role, framework_dispatch, call_construct, plus whatever ADR-0027 Cluster C/D folds produce).\n- Reuse the existing drift / linter / by-axis view machinery; wire producer_coherence.py to walk `meta=` dict-literal arguments.\n\n**ADR-0024 amendment (one paragraph in §\"Scope\"):** explicitly recognize dict-key namespaces as a parallel application of the axis-declaration pattern, pointing forward to ADR-0029 as the first instantiation. Without this amendment, future agents reading ADR-0024 won't connect to ADR-0029.\n\n**WI-vusot's implementation under this framing:**\n1. Open ADR-0029 (Draft) with the worked-example shape above.\n2. Amend ADR-0024 with the scope-clarification paragraph.\n3. Land axis_meta_keys.py registry + drift linter + by-axis view extension.\n4. Extend producer_coherence.py to gate `meta={\"key\": ...}` literal-string emit sites.\n5. Mark ADR-0029 Accepted on Phase 1 land, mirroring ADR-0028's posture.\n6. Phases 2-4 follow the ADR-0028 shape (consumer migration → producer migration → schema deprecation/closure per key as bakeoffs validate).\n\n## Alternatives considered and rejected\n\n**Option A — extend ADR-0024 alone, no new ADR.** Conflates topologically distinct concerns under one document; the five structural differences become invisible to future readers. Rejected.\n\n**Option B — open ADR-0029 alone, no ADR-0024 amendment.** ADR-0024's current scope says \"dataclass fields\"; without an amendment, the connection to ADR-0029 is implicit and easy to miss. Rejected.\n\n**Option D — ship axis_meta_keys.py as an undeclared registry, no ADR.** Loses consistency with sibling axis declarations; future agents won't know whether to fold OR add to the registry. Rejected.\n\n**Option E — fold meta-key registry under ADR-0027 or ADR-0028 (whichever first creates a meta key).** Forces a cross-cutting concern to anchor to one specific axis ADR; creates pressure to decide which ADR \"owns\" the meta-key concept. Rejected.\n\n## Open questions for human triage\n\nThese are not blockers for the recommendation, but worth surfacing:\n\n1. **Per-key value-axis ADRs?** Should each meta key (framework_role, framework_dispatch, call_construct, ...) have its own per-key value-axis ADR (mirroring how ADR-0027 / ADR-0028 are each one-axis-per-ADR), or can a single ADR-0029 enumerate all of them inline? The former is more verbose but cleaner; the latter is more compact but risks scope creep within one ADR.\n\n2. **Edge.meta vs Symbol.meta — shared registry, or separate?** WI-vusot currently bundles both. They have different purpose surfaces (edges carry call-site evidence, symbols carry construct evidence). The case for ONE registry: shared infrastructure, reduced duplication. The case for TWO: clean topology — Edge.meta keys and Symbol.meta keys are distinct namespaces governed by different consumers.\n\n3. **Numbering.** ADR-0029 assumes nothing else takes that number first. If WI-gajob or WI-dubab's audit verdict lands on \"new axis ADR\" before WI-vusot, those would consume ADR-0029 / ADR-0030 first.\n\n## Summary\n\nWI-vusot's implementation should ship ADR-0029 as a small (~1-2 page) ADR following the ADR-0028 shape, plus a one-paragraph amendment to ADR-0024. The audit-question items (WI-gajob, WI-dubab) may file ADRs first depending on their verdicts; if so, WI-vusot's ADR number shifts. The work itself is mechanical once the ADR shape is agreed."  # 32a3
- op: discuss  # 3183
  at: '2026-05-05T01:03:38Z'  # 3183
  by: agent  # 3183
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3183
  clock: 3  # 3183
  nonce: '3183'  # 3183
  message: "## Resolution: open questions extinguished\n\nThe three \"open questions for human triage\" in the prior post were over-deferred. None required human input; all are resolvable from existing pattern. Resolutions below; the implementer should follow these without further triage.\n\n**Q1 — per-key value-axis ADRs (one or N)?** ADR-0029 declares the meta-key namespace + axis_meta_keys.py registry. ADR-0030+ are filed per-key as-needed, when a key's VALUE space accrues enough distinct values to warrant its own declaration. Not all upfront — each per-key ADR earns its filing the same way ADR-0023/0027/0028 did, via an audit revealing axial leakage.\n\n**Q2 — Edge.meta vs Symbol.meta: shared or separate registry?** ONE registry with on-field labels: `MetaKeySpec(name=..., on=\"Edge\"|\"Symbol\", axis=..., ...)`. Three reasons: (a) the concept being declared — \"axis-of-axes for meta dicts\" — generalizes across both, splitting it loses the unifying frame; (b) producer_coherence.py already walks both Edge.create() and Symbol.create() call sites, one registry maps 1:1 onto the existing walker shape; (c) the by-axis view doc shows all meta-key axes in one place. Post-Phase-3 keys don't physically overlap (framework_role only on Symbol, framework_dispatch and call_construct only on Edge), so the on-field label is informational rather than validation-load-bearing.\n\n**Q3 — ADR numbering contention with WI-gajob/WI-dubab?** Non-issue. ADR numbers are assigned at creation time; whatever lands first gets the next available number. No decision required.\n\n## Implementation summary (unambiguous)\n\nWhen WI-vusot's wave comes up:\n1. Open ADR-0029 (Draft) declaring the meta-key namespace convention + axis_meta_keys.py registry shape, modeled on ADR-0028's worked-example shape. One ADR for the namespace; per-key value-axis ADRs come later as-needed.\n2. Amend ADR-0024 with a one-paragraph §\"Scope\" addition recognizing dict-key namespaces as a parallel application, pointing forward to ADR-0029.\n3. Land axis_meta_keys.py with ONE registry containing MetaKeySpec entries for both Edge.meta and Symbol.meta keys, distinguished by an `on` field.\n4. Wire producer_coherence.py to walk `meta={\"key\": ...}` dict-literal arguments at Edge.create() / Symbol.create() call sites.\n5. Land drift linter, property test, by-axis view doc extension.\n6. Mark ADR-0029 Accepted on Phase 1 land. Phases 2-4 follow ADR-0028 shape."  # 3183
